{"t": 1794114398.7720928, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Regression from this change (commit 8c2f1d0): replacing rounding with `int()` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so converted totals come out one minor unit low (expected 1100, got 1099) and reconciliation fails in production.\n\nSentry error: **ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit** \u2014 https://acme.sentry.io/issues/?query=LEDGER-WORKER-9A\n(issue LEDGER-WORKER-9A, first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3, ~2,201 events)\n\nFix: worker/rates.py now rounds again (`return round(amount_minor * rate)`).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
